---
// SafetyNotice: short safety note at the top of every article, before the
// reader tries any exercise. It says plainly that we are not health
// professionals and that readers should check with their own doctor,
// chiropractor or physiotherapist first. The longer MedicalDisclaimer at the
// end of the article stays as it is.
//
// Inside <article class="article-text">, the global reading-text rules skip
// <aside>, so the sizes set here are the ones that apply.
---
<aside
  role="note"
  aria-labelledby="safety-notice-title"
  class="mb-8 rounded-xl border-2 border-amber-300 bg-amber-50 px-4 py-3.5 sm:px-5 sm:py-4"
>
  <div class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
    <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-amber-700 text-2xl shrink-0" aria-hidden="true">health_and_safety</span>
    <div>
      <p id="safety-notice-title" class="font-bold text-base sm:text-lg text-text-main-light mb-1">
        Please read before you start
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm sm:text-base leading-normal text-text-main-light text-pretty mb-1.5">
        We are not doctors, chiropractors or physiotherapists. This page shares
        traditional Japanese practices for general information only. It is not
        medical advice.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm sm:text-base leading-normal text-text-main-light text-pretty">
        <strong>Talk to your doctor, chiropractor or physiotherapist before you
        try anything here</strong>, especially if you have pain, an injury,
        osteoporosis, heart or blood pressure problems, or recent surgery. Move
        gently, and stop straight away if something hurts or you feel dizzy.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</aside>
